 "reconciliation": "SIXTEEN of the seventeen columns this leaf carries a footing for close exactly, residual zero on every one - eight free white female, seven free white male, and the single free coloured figure. ONE does not close and is not forced: m_30_40's footing glyph is not settled, so its printed total is null and the read 18 stands unchecked. THE LEAF FIXES ONE FORM OF THE ENUMERATOR'S ALPHABET AND SEPARATES IT FROM ANOTHER. Printed 213 (T-0963) recorded that this hand writes 4 as two parallel diagonals. On this leaf the two forms stand in the same footing row and are different: m_u5 carries two SEPARATE diagonals of equal length over a column of eleven, while f_5_10 carries a 1 beside a JOINED pair over a column of fourteen and f_40_50 carries the joined pair alone over a column of four. So the disjoint pair is 11 and the joined pair is 4, and printed 213's entry describes the joined form. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK IS NOT EMPTY: one free coloured male under 10 stands on line 1, in the household of E. C. Stowell, and the footing row carries that same single figure and nothing else in any of its twelve columns.",
